{# The one layout every full HTML document on the site extends
   (docs/FRONTEND.md § Server-side templates, issue 241).

   It owns the parts of a document that are the same everywhere — the doctype
   and `<html lang>`, the charset and viewport tags, the brand-asset head
   block, the `<title>`, and the `<style>` element — and leaves four slots:

   - `head_meta`  the page's own description, og/twitter, robots, and canonical
                  tags, written at the head's two-space indent;
   - `styles`     the whole `<style>` element. No page overrides it: since
                  issue 246 a page's own rules live in its own stylesheet,
                  declared as the last part of its CSS entry
                  (rendering/stylesheets.py), so `stylesheet` is already
                  everything the page ships;
   - `body`       everything inside `<body>` except the scripts; and
   - `scripts`    the script slot — a page's client payload element and the one
                  module script that inlines its entry bundle.

   The script slot deliberately lives in each page rather than here. A
   template's inline script is held to a recorded ceiling per template
   (tests/frontend_ratchets.json), and a page that ships no script at all — the
   404 — must be able to record a ceiling of zero rather than inherit a slot it
   does not fill.

   `shell` is an environment global (rendering/documents.py) holding
   `_shell.html.j2`'s macros, so no template has to import the shell to render
   the band, page head, or footer.

   Every page supplies `document_title`, `stylesheet`, and `canonical_origin`.
   `shareable` follows the flag that governs a page's social card (R2) and
   defaults to true; only the 404 sets it false. #}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
{% block head_meta %}{% endblock %}
  {{ shell.head_links(canonical_origin, shareable=shareable | default(true)) }}
  <title>{{ document_title }}</title>
{% block styles %}
  <style>{{ stylesheet | safe }}</style>
{% endblock %}
</head>
<body>
{% block body %}{% endblock %}
{% block scripts %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
